1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,120
FirstEnergy's first-quarter 10-Q credits colder weather:

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,940
heating degree days up 15%.

3
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:08,920
Revenue rose 14.5%.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,930
How much of that was the weather?

5
00:00:11,183 --> 00:00:13,903
The answer: weather is consistent with 8.2

6
00:00:13,923 --> 00:00:15,603
of those points, a bit over half.

7
00:00:16,023 --> 00:00:18,013
Supported, but with a wide range.

8
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:20,547
A solo entry from Singapore.

9
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,860
The analyst picks FirstEnergy, the first quarter of 2025,

10
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,270
and the claim: colder weather.

11
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:32,073
Each chunk streams as the local Nemotron model plans it.

12
00:00:32,453 --> 00:00:34,433
The planner's text is shown as a plan,

13
00:00:34,673 --> 00:00:38,063
never as a fact; only tool rows carry numbers.

14
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,880
Degree days are computed in Lightning SQL,

15
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:43,640
about 20 seconds a quarter;

16
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,270
the whole question takes about two minutes.

17
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,140
On the clean runs, the model's pick matched the

18
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:56,020
checklist's own order in 33 of 34 calls;

19
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:59,590
its real job is valid plans and the memo.

20
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:08,253
Revenue rose 14.5% like for like.

21
00:01:08,793 --> 00:01:11,113
Weather is consistent with 8.2 of those points,

22
00:01:11,273 --> 00:01:12,253
so the claim is supported.

23
00:01:12,773 --> 00:01:16,600
But the range is wide, 1.6 to 14.0:

24
00:01:16,810 --> 00:01:19,413
high confidence means the weather effect is above zero,

25
00:01:19,773 --> 00:01:21,573
not that 8.2 is precise.

26
00:01:22,253 --> 00:01:26,703
Industry-wide, 2.9; company-specific, 3.5.

27
00:01:27,267 --> 00:01:30,600
The filing says heating degree days rose 15%;

28
00:01:30,743 --> 00:01:34,950
the agent's nine stations show total degree days up 16.2%:

29
00:01:35,182 --> 00:01:37,757
a check on a number the agent did not compute.

30
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:40,413
The memo is the model's own writing:

31
00:01:40,953 --> 00:01:42,993
every number in it matched a tool output,

32
00:01:43,253 --> 00:01:46,443
it states the verdict, and it lists what was not tested.

33
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,267
Every figure is a button.

34
00:01:50,807 --> 00:01:53,267
The citation is the Lightning SQL itself,

35
00:01:53,587 --> 00:01:54,967
with its hash, the rows,

36
00:01:55,227 --> 00:01:58,917
the Zetaris object, the endpoint, the licence and the time.

37
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:01,807
A later filing's restatement is recorded,

38
00:02:02,167 --> 00:02:03,387
never applied silently:

39
00:02:04,007 --> 00:02:07,247
at American Electric Power it is 0.4 million,

40
00:02:07,507 --> 00:02:09,627
tiny here, decisive when material.

41
00:02:10,227 --> 00:02:13,497
An override needs a signed, single-use contract.

42
00:02:15,467 --> 00:02:19,287
The same question for Southern Company: revenue rose 17.0%,

43
00:02:19,307 --> 00:02:22,767
and weather is consistent with 6.6 points of it,

44
00:02:22,927 --> 00:02:24,947
so the claim is only partly supported.

45
00:02:25,587 --> 00:02:27,857
The company-specific part is larger.

46
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,560
In Zetaris Lightning, SEC EDGAR is a set of REST

47
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:33,940
tables and NOAA a set of parquet tables;

48
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,900
the semantic layer adds keys and quality rules,

49
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,390
and its coverage result gates the verdict.

50
00:02:39,474 --> 00:02:43,444
At onboarding, that rule checked 342 rows: all valid.

51
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,500
The footer is measured: eight planner calls,

52
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:49,750
one of them repaired, no fallbacks, and zero cloud calls.

53
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:52,313
One data path, through Zetaris.

54
00:02:52,693 --> 00:02:56,013
Meterless engines run the chain, the memory and the world model;

55
00:02:56,433 --> 00:02:59,223
Nemotron plans and writes on one local GPU.

56
00:03:00,033 --> 00:03:03,793
Measured: 171 of 171 claims cited,

57
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:07,403
one card from five runs, zero cloud calls.

58
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:08,960
Weather-or-Not.

59
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:12,190
Every number is cited, and every override is signed.
